new push to help fight the coronavirus  americans can now order free at home  coveted tests through a government  website called  covidtest.gov  it's part of president biden's promise  to improve testing as the omicron  variant spreads but critics say it is  not nearly enough ed o'keefe is at the  white house for us ed good morning to  you new government website does not  always inspire confidence what do we  know well good morning as you said every  person now can order up to four free  tests for a residential address the  website name bears repeating  covatests.gov  has been eagerly anticipated ever since  president biden announced a plan in  december to ship half a billion at-home  tests to americans last week the  president doubled the country's order  with plans now to eventually provide a  billion of them to households nationwide  the website had a soft launch yesterday  and there were isolated reports of  problems with the address verification  part but no significant issues have been  reported as of this morning and once  tests are ordered it won't be a rapid  turnaround officials say the u.s postal  service typically ships the tests within  7 to 12 days this comes as the biden  administration is also announcing plans  this morning to start shipping 400  million n95 masks starting at the end of  this week they're coming out of the  strategic national stockpile and will be  available at community health centers  and pharmacies across the country where  millions are already getting tested and  receiving vaccines we'll get more  details on this later today when the  president holds his first solo news  conference of the year  thank you so much
 

